dir/posix
description: Directory with case-sensitive filenames
- >
  On a POSIX filesystem the filenames - hence the KEYS - are CASE SENSITIVE: `Readme` and
  `readme` are two different entries, and keys compare byte-exactly. With the control `.yo`
  subdirectory it becomes the overlay concrete - see the subchapter below:
- *: 00-dir_posix_yo
